{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ufwn4loqtzx52qqql2cb3bsr7sjab5esutmzjzthir6qv4rfomaq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green. Done.\n\n## Report\n\n**Deliverables (all written)**\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-s3DwgU/translation/tests/h2c.rs` — 18 tests, **all passing**\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-s3DwgU/_v/configs/h2c.md` — **31** config rows, all `[x]`\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-s3DwgU/_v/errors/h2c.md` — **16** error rows (12 `[x]`, 4 `[abort]`)\n\n**Counts:** 31 config rows / 16 error rows / 18 tests / all passing. `ed25519low.rs` and `smoke.rs` also still pass after my one src edit.\n\n**Symbols covered:** `_sodium_core_h2c_string_to_hash`, `crypto_core_ed25519_from_string`, `crypto_core_ed25519_from_string_nu`, `crypto_core_ed25519_scalar_from_string`, `crypto_core_ristretto255_from_string`, `crypto_core_ristretto255_scalar_from_string`, `crypto_core_ristretto255_from_hash`, `_sodium_ge25519_from_uniform`, `_sodium_ge25519_from_hash`, `_sodium_ristretto255_from_hash`.\nNote: `crypto_core_ed25519_from_string_ro` / `crypto_core_ed25519_from_uniform` / `crypto_core_ed25519_from_hash` **do not exist** in this libsodium version (`_v/persym.txt` only has `from_string` and `from_string_nu`).\n\n**Divergence found and fixed (1)**\n- `_sodium_core_h2c_string_to_hash` with `h_len > 0xff`. The C has `assert(h_len <= 0xff)` in *both* static helpers (`core_h2c.c:26`, `core_h2c.c:82`), and the reference build has asserts **live** (`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` is empty ⇒ no `-DNDEBUG`; `U __assert_fail` is present in `core_h2c.c.o`). C aborts (SIGABRT / exit 134); the Rust had no check and returned 0 after writing `h_len` bytes with `t[1] = h_len as u8` (so e.g. `h_len=256` produced 256 bytes of a *different*, non-abort output).\n  Fix: two 3-line guards in `translation/src/core_ed25519.rs` (`if h_len > 0xff { crate::csys::abort(); }`), matching the house style of the `_string_to_points` `n > 2` abort. Verified out-of-process with a throwaway `dlopen` probe: `alg∈{1,2} × h_len∈{256,1000}` → exit 134 in *both* libs; `h_len=255` → identical output in both. Not testable in-process (`panic = \"abort\"` test binary).\n\n**Notable C quirks explicitly exercised and confirmed byte-identical**\n- `ctx_len > 0xff` \"H2C-OVERSIZE-DST-\" pre-hash branch, *including* the aliasing subtlety that `ctx` is repointed at `u0`, and `u0` is then overwritten by the main hash before the per-block loop re-reads it as the DST. Both libs alias identically.\n- `t[1] = (unsigned char) h_len` and the partial tail `memcpy(&h[i], ux, min(sizeof ux, h_len - i))` — canary-verified that nothing past `h_len` is written.\n- `hash_alg` default branch sets `errno = EINVAL (22)` — asserted on the real process errno (poisoned to ENOENT first) for 11 out-of-range ids × 6 `h_len`s, and that the output buffer is left fully untouched.\n- `NULL` tolerance: `h=NULL` with `h_len=0`, and `ctx`/`msg = NULL` with length 0 (safe because both `crypto_hash_sha{256,512}_update` early-return on `inlen==0`).\n- In-place aliasing of `_sodium_ge25519_from_uniform(s, s)` (legal via the leading `memcpy(s,r,32)`) and `crypto_core_ristretto255_from_hash(p, p)`.\n- Layer-composition cross-checks (C-vs-C and Rust-vs-Rust) proving `from_string == add(from_hash(rev48(h[0..48])), from_hash(rev48(h[48..96])))` and `ristretto255_from_string == ristretto255_from_hash(h2c(64))` — this is what catches a wrong big-endian reversal or zero-padding of the 48→64-byte buffer.\n\n**Not verified / caveats**\n- The three `[abort]` rows other than E2/E3 are unreachable and checked only by inspection: `_string_to_points` `n > 2` (no public caller passes n>2) and `ge25519_elligator2`'s `ge25519_xmont_to_ymont != 0` abort (mathematically unreachable; never hit in 140 tested inputs). Both are present in the Rust as `crate::csys::abort()`.\n- `crypto_core_ed25519_from_string`'s tail `return crypto_core_ed25519_add(...)` cannot be made to fail (both operands come from `ge25519_from_hash`); I asserted `rc == 0` over 300+ inputs and verified by inspection that the Rust propagates `add`'s return value.\n- Test harness note: `cargo test --test h2c --target-dir _t/h2c` does **not** emit the cdylib into `_t/h2c`; the harness falls back to `translation/target/release/liblibsodium.so`. I ran `cargo build --release --offline` first, so the tested `.so` includes my fix — but any agent running only `cargo test` with a private target-dir is testing whatever is in `translation/target/release`.\n- I did not touch `translation/src/ed25519_ref10_ristretto.rs`; I read it line-by-line against `ed25519_ref10.c:2590-2992` and found no divergence (the `optblocker`, `unsigned char` truncations in `ristretto255_is_canonical`, and the `38 * fe_g[i]` / `*19` / `*722` terms in `fe25519_reduce64` are all faithfully reproduced). No edit conflicts with the `ed25519low` agent occurred."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":123369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":446,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Jmh96EwTpBnU2Bi86QVUwn","session_id":"f6aed658-f045-47ac-a150-aec5e315d5dc","uuid":"798e9716-fa9b-4155-ad4d-1fa8f6964483","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:40:59.809Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Add core_h2c coverage to ed25519low"}
