{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_w54woiybgwhem3f2xpqdlctddrd6at6ko3khvto43jsxgnqk63sq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All deliverables are in place and passing. Final summary:\n\n## Counts\n- **Config rows:** 42 (`_v/configs/aead2.md`) — all `[x]`\n- **Error rows:** 31 (`_v/errors/aead2.md`) — 27 `[x]`, 4 `[abort]`\n- **Tests:** 16 `#[test]` functions in `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-s3DwgU/translation/tests/aead2.rs`, **all 16 pass** (`cargo test --release --offline --target-dir $W/_t/aead2 --test aead2 -- --test-threads=1`, 1.6 s)\n- Every symbol listed for my four object files in `_v/persym.txt` is exercised (16 × `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_*`, 11 × `crypto_aead_aegis128l_*` incl. `_pick_best_implementation` and the `aegis128l_soft_implementation` data object, 11 × `crypto_aead_aegis256_*` likewise, and all 9 `_sodium_softaes_*`).\n\n## Ground-truth facts pinned by the tests\n- With no `HAVE_*` macros, `aead_aes256gcm.c` compiles the **stub branch**: `is_available()` → `0`, and all 9 crypto entry points do exactly `errno = ENOSYS (38); return -1;` writing **nothing** (verified with canary buffers, including the 512-byte state passed to `beforenm`). `statebytes()` = 512 on both.\n- `softaes.c` compiles the non-`FAVOR_PERFORMANCE` **SRM-1R bitsliced** `softaes_block_encrypt` (verified by the `#else` branch semantics matching, plus a FIPS-197 C.1 KAT run independently against *both* libraries so the tests pin real AES, not just C↔Rust agreement).\n- `_crypto_aead_aegis*_pick_best_implementation()` always selects the soft impl and returns 0.\n\n## Rust divergences found\n**None.** All four assigned modules (`aead_aes256gcm.rs`, `aead_aegis128l.rs`, `aead_aegis256.rs`, `softaes.rs`) are byte-exact against the C for every case tested; I made **no functional edits** to any `src/*.rs`.\n\nI validated that the tests are actually sensitive with a negative control: injecting `tmp.w0 ^= 1` into `aegis256_enc` made `aegis256_public_api` and `aegis256_soft_implementation_object` fail with a byte-diff (`C = a81d… / Rust = a91d…`); the injection was then removed and the file restored (verified: no `tmp.w0` occurrence remains, all tests green again).\n\n## One non-behavioural difference (reported, deliberately not \"fixed\")\n`aegis128l_soft_implementation` / `aegis256_soft_implementation` are non-`const` in C and land in `.data` (writable); the Rust `#[no_mangle] pub static` versions land in `.data.rel.ro`, which the loader makes read-only after relocation. Symbol size (16 B) and contents match, and libsodium never writes through these objects, so no observable behaviour differs — but an external consumer writing to the symbol would succeed against the C `.so` and fault against the Rust one. Changing it to `static mut` would require `addr_of!` gymnastics for the `IMPLEMENTATION` initializer with zero behavioural gain, so I left it.\n\n## Not verified / limitations\n- **`sodium_misuse()` paths** (`aead2-E12`…`E15`: `mlen`/`adlen > MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` in `crypto_aead_aegis{128l,256}_encrypt` and `_encrypt_detached`) abort the process, so they are marked `[abort]` and verified only by source inspection — the Rust calls `sodium_misuse()` at the identical point with the identical comparison, and (matching C) writes `*maclen_p` *before* the check in `_encrypt_detached`.\n- `keygen` is only comparable after injecting a deterministic `randombytes_implementation` into both libraries (`randombytes_set_implementation`); with the real RNG only the write extent can be checked. The test does both.\n- `crypto_aead_aegis*_decrypt` with `clen` in the range where `clen - ABYTES` is still ≤ `MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` but astronomically large cannot be tested (it would try to read 2^61 bytes); only the forwarded-rejection variants (`u64::MAX`, `2^61-1+33`) are covered.\n- `cargo test` does **not** rebuild the cdylib; `cargo build --release --offline --target-dir <dir>` must be run first for the same `--target-dir`. Worth noting for whoever re-runs these."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":298,"cache_read_input_tokens":203117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":298,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01NTqZSYuwFhtpRjUrbynVyW","session_id":"f6aed658-f045-47ac-a150-aec5e315d5dc","uuid":"e8fbdcca-4384-493d-9ef4-6738bfe39b3e","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:42:43.694Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Verify aes-gcm/aegis area"}
