{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xlmv47eo7v5l6ok6xszs3idtep6n3nfp2rddhhr2ecbftlpz4bja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All done. Final verification run passes.\n\n## Report\n\n**Deliverables**\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-s3DwgU/translation/tests/stream.rs` — 21 tests, **all passing**\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-s3DwgU/_v/configs/stream.md` — **68 config rows**, all `[x]`\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-s3DwgU/_v/errors/stream.md` — **25 error rows**: 18 `[x]`, 7 `[abort]`\n\n**Symbol coverage:** all 87 exported symbols from the area's object files are exercised, including both implementation structs (`crypto_stream_salsa20_ref_implementation`, `crypto_stream_chacha20_ref_implementation` — every function pointer inside is fetched via `both_data!` and called through both libraries) and `_crypto_stream_{salsa20,chacha20}_pick_best_implementation`. The 20 `crypto_core_*_{output,input,key,const}bytes` getters are resolved through a `format!`-built name helper (they'd panic if absent), so a literal grep of the test file doesn't show them.\n\n**Divergences found: none.** The Rust in `crypto_stream.rs`, `stream_salsa20.rs`, `stream_chacha20.rs`, `core_salsa.rs`, `core_hsalsa20.rs`, `core_hchacha20.rs` is byte-exact against the C for every input tried. No Rust source changes were needed.\n\n**Non-vacuity proof (mutation test):** I temporarily injected 4 bugs (salsa208 rounds 8→10; hchacha20 10→9 double-rounds; chacha `if (!j12) j13++` overflow branch disabled; salsa20 `ic` byte-splat loop shortened to 8..15) and rebuilt. Exactly the expected 12 tests failed and the 9 unaffected ones passed. Reverted; the rebuilt `.so` is now **byte-identical** to the pristine prebuilt `translation/target/release/liblibsodium.so`, confirming a clean revert.\n\n**Notable coverage details**\n- Counter overflow is genuinely exercised, not just nominally: 