) Notable methodology / things not verified\n- **Harness gotcha worth relaying to the other agents:** `cargo test --target-dir <dir> --test <area>` does **not** build the cdylib into `<dir>`, so `common::rust_so_path()` silently falls back to `translation/target/release/liblibsodium.so` — i.e. you test a *stale* Rust library and mutations go undetected. I caught this with a deliberate mutation (changing `crypto_verify_16_bytes` to 15 produced a green run). You must run `cargo build --release --offline --target-dir <dir>` **first**. I re-ran everything after fixing this, and also refreshed `translation/target/release/liblibsodium.so`.\n- **Abort paths are actually tested**, not just inspected: `abort_paths` re-executes the test binary as a child process for 37 misuse/assert cases × both libraries (74 spawns) and asserts each dies with `SIGABRT`. This is what surfaced the divergence above. It costs ~75 s of the run.\n- **State-layout comparison**: `blake2b_state` is `#pragma pack(1)` in C (361 bytes, no padding) and `repr(C)` in Rust (identical field offsets), so I compare the full 384-byte opaque buffer after init / every update / final. Same for the 208/416-byte hkdf states. No \"compare digest only\" concessions were needed anywhere.\n- **`blake2-E64` (`_sodium_blake2b_long` with `outlen > UINT32_MAX`)** is the only row I could not test: it needs a >4 GiB output buffer. Verified by inspection that the Rust `break 'fail` leaves `ret = -1`, matching the C `goto fail`.\n- `*_keygen` functions use `randombytes_buf`, so their bytes are inherently incomparable; I verified only that exactly KEYBYTES are written and the canary past the end is intact.\n- The 12 `[dead]` error rows are branches that provably cannot fire in this build (`inlen > UINT64_MAX` on a `uint64_t`; `assert`s guarded by an earlier `return -1`; `LCOV_EXCL_LINE` `init*() != 0` checks where the callee only returns 0 or aborts; `assert(S->buflen <= 128)` after subtracting 128 from a value in 129..256). I marked them `[dead]` rather than `[x]` to avoid claiming coverage I don't have."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":195214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":765,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01H9nfiHsfbfhEQtqWpWwm7h","session_id":"f6aed658-f045-47ac-a150-aec5e315d5dc","uuid":"89bd65d3-13cc-48e7-b779-06c08c039323","timestamp":"2026-09-04T03:48:30.967Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Verify blake2b/kdf/shorthash/verify"}
