{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_75gd2me4klk5itm4ofetasib5bmyumhthy4j6c2idv6mmsu4psea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — all four gates pass.**\n\n## Results\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — symbol parity | **890 C exports / 890 Rust exports, 0 missing, 0 extra.** All undefined symbols in the Rust `.so` resolve to glibc/libgcc |\n| Phase B — `CONFIGS.md` | **686 / 686** configuration rows pass across randomized inputs (fixed seed) |\n| Phase C — `ERRORS.md` | **600 rows, 0 open.** 490 have an executing differential test; the rest are dead/unreachable/not-compiled/needs->4 GiB, each with a stated reason |\n| Feature combos | Crate has **no `[features]`** and no `cfg(feature…)` — one build config. Verified: default, `--no-default-features`, `--all-features` all give **238 passed / 0 failed** |\n\n## Test suite\n`translation/tests/` — 14 files, 238 tests, all loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading` (`c_src/build/libsodium.so` + `target/release/liblibsodium.so`); no Rust function is ever called directly.\n\n## Bugs found in the Rust and fixed\nThe reference C build compiles with **no `-DNDEBUG`**, so C `assert()` is live (`__assert_fail` is in the C `.so`) — three real divergences came from that plus one from Rust enum niche optimisation:\n\n1. **`argon2_type` modelled as a Rust `enum`** (`argon2.rs`, `argon2_encoding.rs`, `pwhash_argon2.rs`) — rustc knew the range was `1..=2` and deleted the C's `default:`/`else` arms. `_sodium_argon2_ctx(&ctx, 0)` returned `0` and hashed with a bogus type where C returns `-26`. Fixed by using `c_int` + consts.\n2. **`crypto_generichash_blake2b_final` with `outlen > 255`** (`blake2b.rs`) — Rust truncated to `u8` and returned a 44-byte digest; C aborts.\n3. **`_sodium_core_h2c_string_to_hash` with `h_len > 0xff`** (`core_ed25519.rs`) — Rust returned 0 with different output; C aborts.\n4. **Dropped `assert()`s in `randombytes_sysrandom.rs` / `randombytes_internal.rs` / `sodium_codecs.rs`** — reachable via `randombytes_sysrandom_implementation.buf(p, 0)`: C aborts, Rust returned normally.\n\n## Anti-vacuity evidence (run by me, not self-reported)\nSix independent single-token mutations of the Rust (SHA-512 round constant, AES S-box byte, salsa20 counter byte, scrypt constant, poly1305 pad mask, hex-encode constant) were each caught — together they made **all 12 area suites** fail; sources were then restored byte-identical (`diff -r` clean) and the full suite is green again.\n\nReachable `sodium_misuse()`/`assert()` paths are tested **out of process** (`tests/gaps.rs::abort_parity`, 34 cases × 2 libraries) asserting both children die with SIGABRT — this also closed 21 rows the area agents had left as inspection-only, plus `blake2-E64` which was closed with an in-process test."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2008,"cache_read_input_tokens":216254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2008,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6aed658-f045-47ac-a150-aec5e315d5dc","uuid":"924bed76-58bd-4a6c-a30b-8834a8586482","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:42:30.860Z"}
